+# Agent Note: Inclusive tool schema unions
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-13-inclusive-tool-schema-unions.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A JavaScript or TypeScript union accepts a value that belongs to more than one member. Exact-one JSON Schema unions reject those values, so dynamic tool declarations need an inclusive union that the registry, validator and type renderers all understand.
+
+## Decision
+
+The raw schema and author DSL support anyOf alongside oneOf. Both require at least two branches and allow annotations without sibling type constraints. Validation accepts one or more anyOf matches and exactly one oneOf match. The TypeScript and Python SDK renderers project either construct as a language union; runtime validation retains the distinction.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Converting every union to oneOf changes acceptance for overlapping members. Replacing the output schema with unconstrained JSON removes validation and type information. A consumer-owned validator would leave the registry unable to register its actual schema. The shared subset therefore owns inclusive validation as well as its declarations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Existing oneOf semantics remain exact-one. Unsupported keywords and invalid combinations still fail at registration. Schema tests cover overlap, zero matches and malformed branches; the recorded union-tool-schema Session pins the native declaration. No Session event or Agent Loop stage changes.
